<% content_for :page_header do %>
  <h1>About</h1>
<% end %>

<% page_nav [["Backstory", "/about#about-backstory"],
             ["Contact", "/about#about-contact"]] %>

<div class="row row-odd">
  <div class="page">
    <div id="about-backstory" class="columns">
      <div class="second-column sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-container">
          <h2>Developer</h2>
          <div class="headshot-image-wrapper">
            <div class="image">
              <img src="/images/headshot-scaled.png" alt="Headshot">
            </div>
            <p class="image-label">Darrell Sandstrom</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            Ten+ years of experience writing software mostly for web apps. Specialized in Ruby
            backend, however proficient in CSS and JavaScript.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="first-column">
        <h2>Backstory</h2>
        <p>
          While working as an engineer for a marketing firm, one of my responsibilities was
          selecting and setting up issue tracking and task management software. I tried and
          used many options and eventually settled on <strong>Jira</strong>. I setup the configurations for the
          company including custom workflows, user management, and the issue/question portal.
          It's decent software, however, it's overly complicated and difficult to debug. I
          wanted to make something better and <strong>open source</strong>. So I've spent much
          time contemplating what I like best about the software I've used and ported that
          into <strong>TaskRoller</strong>. In addition, I copied the workflow that I setup
          and hard-wired that into my App.
        </p>

        <p>
          A major difference with Jira, besides being free and open source, is the workflows
          are not customizable. The App uses the <strong>"Convention over
          Configuration"</strong> approach. I feel like the workflows I've used for Issues and
          Tasks fit for most companies that write software. However, I'm open to improvements
          and the App is not feature
          complete. Yet I use tried and tested Ruby gems including
          <a href="https://github.com/heartcombo/devise" target="_remote">Devise</a>
          for authentication and
          <a href="https://github.com/coorasse/cancancan" target="_remote">CanCanCan</a>
          for authorization. In addition, I use
          <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/" target="_remote">PostgreSQL</a>
          for the database and
          <a href="https://github.com/puma/puma" target="_remote">Puma</a>
           for the web server. The App is fully tested by me and has a full suite of RSpec tests
           to ensure reliability and allow future refactoring.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row row-even">
  <div class="page">
    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <div id="about-contact" class="columns">
      <section class="second-column sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-container">
          <p>
            Send an <strong>email</strong> to the developer by using the form. Alternatively, view the
            <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller/" target="_blank">source code</a>
            or submit an bug report on <strong>GitHub</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="first-column">
        <%= form_errors @email_message %>
        <form id="contact-form" class="contact-form" name="contact_form" action="/contact"
              method="post" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[loaded_at]" id="contact_loaded_at"
                 value="<%= Time.now.utc %>">
          <div class="field">
            <div class="field-label-and-message">
              <label for="contact[name]">Your Name</label>
              <span class=field-message></span>
            </div>
            <input type="text" name="contact[name]" id="contact_name"
                   value="<%= @email_message.name %>">
          </div>

          <div class="field hide">
            <div class="field-label-and-message">
              <label for="contact[title]">Title</label>
              <span class=field-message></span>
            </div>
            <input type="text" name="contact[title]" id="contact_title"
                   tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true"
                   value="<%= @email_message.title %>">
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <div class="field-label-and-message">
              <label for="contact[return_email]">Your Email</label>
              <span class=field-message></span>
            </div>
            <input type="email" name="contact[return_email]" id="contact_return_email"
                   value="<%= @email_message.return_email %>">
          </div>

          <div class="field">
            <div class="field-label-and-message">
              <label for="contact[body]">Question or Comment</label>
              <span class=field-message></span>
            </div>
            <textarea name="contact[body]" id="contact_body"><%= @email_message.body %></textarea>
          </div>

          <div class="actions">
            <input type="submit" value="Send Email">
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
